From 840bcf962e34bcf76938edf471accb1dc3b51222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mymes1 <203492482+mymes1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:33:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enable real freeform windows on Samsung firmware without DeX

Dextop opened every application fullscreen in its virtual desktop on a
Galaxy Tab A9 (SM-X110, Android 15). Two defects combined:

* DeviceProfiles resolved every Samsung device to the DeX profile, which
  is platformManaged, applies no desktop globals and does not configure
  windowing. On firmware without a DeX desktop nothing configured it.
* The only display-windowing switch Dextop used,
  `wm set-display-windowing-mode`, was added in Android 16, so all three
  of its shell strategies failed on API 35 and looked like a policy
  refusal.

The profile is now chosen from the firmware's actual window stack, the
display is switched through IWindowManager#setWindowingMode (present
since Android 12, wrapped by the Android 16 command), and the result is
read back instead of assumed. Launches always request a freeform window,
and the resulting task is verified and repaired once if the framework
produced a fullscreen task. The Android 16 shell commands are only used
on Android 16+.

Verified by type-checking the windowing sources against the API 35
android.jar and by 22 unit tests (DeviceMatchTest, DisplayWindowingTest).
docs/freeform-windowing.md documents the root cause, the patch, the
device procedure, the test matrix, the limitations and the rollback.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
